(PRC-27, PRC-28: `Create symbolic link from '<target>' to "<linkpath>".`
 performs symlink(2) - the SECOND path is the link created, and it
 points at the FIRST (LANGUAGE.md:4270); sets the error flag on failure
 (LANGUAGE.md:4271). Hand-verified gotcha this session, not in the
 manual: a relative TARGET resolves relative to the LINK's own
 directory, not the process's cwd, so writing the target as a full
 scratch-relative path double-prefixes and dangles. The retained probe
 (docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-27.vox) already avoids this by
 giving `target` as a bare filename, sibling to the link in the same
 scratch directory; this leaf does the same. Confined to the per-run
 scratch directory; stands aside the same way as the directory leaves
 above.)
To 'gen leaf process symbolic link' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    If gen_does_file_io is false then,
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    If gen_scratch_flag is empty then,
        Print "PROBE PRC-27: gen_does_file_io true but gen_scratch_flag unbound",
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    Set gen_file_ios to gen_file_ios add 1.
    a text called 'the payload path' is 'gen process witness'.
    a number called 'the path number' is gen_buffer_names.
    a text called 'the bare payload name' is "procpayload{'the path number'}".
    a text called 'the payload line' is "a text called {'the payload path'} is \"{{{gen_scratch_flag}}}/{'the bare payload name'}\"".
    a text called 'the handle name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "scribe".
    a text called 'the open line' is "open a file for writing called {'the handle name'} at {'the payload path'}".
    a text called 'the write line' is "Write \"payload\" to {'the handle name'}".
    a text called 'the close line' is "Close {'the handle name'}".
    a text called 'the link path name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "link path".
    a text called 'the link path line' is "a text called {'the link path name'} is \"{{{gen_scratch_flag}}}/proclink{'the path number'}\"".
    a text called 'the create link' is "Create symbolic link from \"{'the bare payload name'}\" to {'the link path name'}".
    a text called 'the resolves assert' is "If {'the link path name'} is not available then, Print \"ASSERT PRC-27: expected available got missing\", Exit 95. Print \"resolves\"".
    a text called 'the missing target name' is "procmissing{'the path number'}".
    a text called 'the dangling path name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "dangling path".
    a text called 'the dangling path line' is "a text called {'the dangling path name'} is \"{{{gen_scratch_flag}}}/procdangling{'the path number'}\"".
    a text called 'the create dangling' is "Create symbolic link from \"{'the missing target name'}\" to {'the dangling path name'}".
    a text called 'the dangles assert' is "If {'the dangling path name'} is available then, Print \"ASSERT PRC-27: expected missing got available\", Exit 95. Print \"dangling\"".
    a text called 'the duplicate flag' is 'gen buffer companion' of "already exists".
    a text called 'the duplicate flag init' is "a boolean called {'the duplicate flag'} is false".
    a text called 'the create duplicate' is "Create symbolic link from \"{'the missing target name'}\" to {'the dangling path name'}".
    a text called 'the duplicate handler' is "On error Set {'the duplicate flag'} to true".
    a text called 'the duplicate assert' is 'gen assert true' of "PRC-28" and 'the duplicate flag'.
    a text called 'the cleanup link' is "Delete the file {'the link path name'}".
    a text called 'the cleanup dangling' is "Delete the file {'the dangling path name'}".
    a text called 'the cleanup payload' is "Delete the file {'the payload path'}".
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the payload line', 'the open line', 'the write line', 'the close line', 'the link path line', 'the create link', 'the resolves assert', 'the dangling path line', 'the create dangling', 'the dangles assert', 'the duplicate flag init', 'the create duplicate', 'the duplicate handler', 'the duplicate assert', 'the cleanup link', 'the cleanup dangling', 'the cleanup payload'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(PRC-42, PRC-43, PRC-44, PRC-46: fork/reap are EXPRESSIONS, not
 statements - usable anywhere an expression is valid, not only after
 `Set` (LANGUAGE.md:4326-4327). `fork the process`/bare `fork` both work
 (LANGUAGE.md:4329-4330, the trailing `the process` is optional); fork
 returns 0 in the child, the child's real pid in the parent
 (LANGUAGE.md:4330-4331); `reap any child process` (wait4 pid -1)
 returns the reaped child's pid (LANGUAGE.md:4332-4333). Two shapes are
 drawn: the ordinary `a number called ... is fork ...` form (varying the
 fork spelling, asserting the reaped pid equals the forked one), and
 fork used DIRECTLY as an If-condition with no intermediate `Set` at
 all, hand-verified this session to fork correctly there too (the
 child's branch still runs, the parent's does not) - the
 expression-position claim at the boundary the manual actually names.
 The second shape has no captured pid to compare against, so it asserts
 the weaker but still real property PRC-44 documents: the parent
 successfully reaps a positive pid.)
To 'gen leaf process fork reap basic' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    Set gen_process_has_reaped to true.
    a number called 'the shape draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a number called 'the spelling draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a text called 'the fork expr' is "fork the process".
    If 'the spelling draw' is 1 then,
        Set 'the fork expr' to "fork".
    a number called 'the exit code' is 'gen process safe exit code'.
    If 'the shape draw' is 0 then,
        a text called 'the child name' is 'gen process witness',
        a text called 'the reaped name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "reaped pid",
        a text called 'the fork line' is "a number called {'the child name'} is {'the fork expr'}",
        a text called 'the child branch' is "If {'the child name'} is 0 then, Exit {'the exit code'}",
        a text called 'the reap line' is "a number called {'the reaped name'} is reap any child process",
        a text called 'the matched name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "reap matched",
        a text called 'the matched init' is "a boolean called {'the matched name'} is false",
        a text called 'the matched set' is "If {'the reaped name'} is {'the child name'} then, Set {'the matched name'} to true",
        a text called 'the assert line' is 'gen assert true' of "PRC-46" and 'the matched name',
        a list called 'the lines set form' is ['the fork line', 'the child branch', 'the reap line', 'the matched init', 'the matched set', 'the assert line'],
        'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines set form'.
    If 'the shape draw' is 1 then,
        a text called 'the reaped name' is 'gen process witness',
        a text called 'the condition line' is "If fork the process is 0 then, Exit {'the exit code'}",
        a text called 'the reap line' is "a number called {'the reaped name'} is reap any child process",
        a text called 'the flag name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "reap succeeded",
        a text called 'the flag init' is "a boolean called {'the flag name'} is false",
        a text called 'the flag set' is "If {'the reaped name'} is greater than 0 then, Set {'the flag name'} to true",
        a text called 'the assert line' is 'gen assert true' of "PRC-42" and 'the flag name',
        a list called 'the lines expr form' is ['the condition line', 'the reap line', 'the flag init', 'the flag set', 'the assert line'],
        'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines expr form'.

(PRC-56, PRC-57, PRC-58: `the reaped status` yields the raw wait4
 status word, undecoded (LANGUAGE.md:4374-4375) - an exit code times
 256, hand-verified. It reflects only the most recent SUCCESSFUL reap:
 a reap that fails (ECHILD, on a pid this program never forked) leaves
 it exactly where it was (LANGUAGE.md:4376). Before any successful reap
 anywhere in the whole program it is the sentinel `-1`
 (LANGUAGE.md:4377-4378) - but that claim is only true the FIRST time a
 program reaps, and four other kinds in this file (264, 266, 267, 268)
 can each reap too, so this leaf only claims the sentinel when
 gen_process_has_reaped says nothing has reaped yet; otherwise it still
 exercises the decode-then-fails-to-disturb-it half, just without the
 specific `-1` claim.)
To 'gen leaf process reaped status decode' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a boolean called 'the is first reap' is false.
    If gen_process_has_reaped is false then,
        Set 'the is first reap' to true.
    Set gen_process_has_reaped to true.
    a number called 'the exit code' is 'gen process safe exit code'.
    a text called 'the child name' is 'gen process witness'.
    a text called 'the child line' is "a number called {'the child name'} is fork the process".
    a text called 'the child branch' is "If {'the child name'} is 0 then, Exit {'the exit code'}".
    a text called 'the reap name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "reap result".
    a text called 'the reap line' is "a number called {'the reap name'} is reap child {'the child name'}".
    a text called 'the decoded name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "decoded exit".
    a text called 'the decode line' is "a number called {'the decoded name'} is the reaped status divide 256 modulo 256".
    a text called 'the decode assert' is 'gen assert number is' of "PRC-56" and 'the decoded name' and 'the exit code'.
    a number called 'the foreign pid' is 'rng below' of 900000 add 9000000.
    a text called 'the foreign reap name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "foreign reap".
    a text called 'the foreign reap line' is "a number called {'the foreign reap name'} is reap process {'the foreign pid'}".
    a text called 'the foreign flag name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "reap failed".
    a text called 'the foreign flag init' is "a boolean called {'the foreign flag name'} is false".
    a text called 'the foreign handler' is "On error Set {'the foreign flag name'} to true".
    a text called 'the foreign flag assert' is 'gen assert true' of "PRC-49" and 'the foreign flag name'.
    a text called 'the still decoded name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "still decoded".
    a text called 'the redecode line' is "a number called {'the still decoded name'} is the reaped status divide 256 modulo 256".
    a text called 'the redecode assert' is 'gen assert number is' of "PRC-57" and 'the still decoded name' and 'the exit code'.
    If 'the is first reap' then,
        a text called 'the sentinel assert' is 'gen assert number is' of "PRC-58" and "the reaped status" and -1,
        a list called 'the lines with sentinel' is ['the sentinel assert', 'the child line', 'the child branch', 'the reap line', 'the decode line', 'the decode assert', 'the foreign flag init', 'the foreign reap line', 'the foreign handler', 'the foreign flag assert', 'the redecode line', 'the redecode assert'],
        'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines with sentinel'.
    If 'the is first reap' is false then,
        a list called 'the lines plain' is ['the child line', 'the child branch', 'the reap line', 'the decode line', 'the decode assert', 'the foreign flag init', 'the foreign reap line', 'the foreign handler', 'the foreign flag assert', 'the redecode line', 'the redecode assert'],
        'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines plain'.

(PRC-62, PRC-63: the compiler has no wait-status decoding built in - a
 program decodes the raw word with `divide`, `modulo` and `bit-and`,
 with nothing installed (LANGUAGE.md:4391-4394). The manual's own worked
 decoder functions, `'exit code of'` and `'signal of'`
 (LANGUAGE.md:4397-4401), compile and return the exit code and
 terminating signal; this leaf declares them ONCE per program (a second
 declaration is a duplicate-label assembly error, hand-verified this
 session) and cross-checks their output against the same divide/modulo/
 bit-and the manual shows underneath them - two ways of reading the same
 word must agree, and both must agree with the exit code the generator
 actually chose.)
To 'gen leaf process status decode functions' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    If gen_process_decoders_declared is false then,
        a text called 'the exit decoder' is "{indent}To 'exit code of' with a number called status.\n{indent}    Return a number, status divide 256 modulo 256.\n\n",
        a text called 'the signal decoder' is "{indent}To 'signal of' with a number called status.\n{indent}    Return a number, status bit-and 127.\n\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the exit decoder',
        'gen emit' of 'the signal decoder',
        Set gen_process_decoders_declared to true.
    Set gen_process_has_reaped to true.
    a number called 'the exit code' is 'gen process safe exit code'.
    a text called 'the child name' is 'gen process witness'.
    a text called 'the child line' is "a number called {'the child name'} is fork the process".
    a text called 'the child branch' is "If {'the child name'} is 0 then, Exit {'the exit code'}".
    a text called 'the reap name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "decode reap".
    a text called 'the reap line' is "a number called {'the reap name'} is reap child {'the child name'}".
    a text called 'the status name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "status word".
    a text called 'the status line' is "a number called {'the status name'} is the reaped status".
    a text called 'the manual exit name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "manual exit".
    a text called 'the manual exit line' is "a number called {'the manual exit name'} is {'the status name'} divide 256 modulo 256".
    a text called 'the function exit name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "function exit".
    a text called 'the function exit line' is "a number called {'the function exit name'} is 'exit code of' of {'the status name'}".
    a text called 'the exit agree assert' is 'gen assert number matches' of "PRC-63" and 'the function exit name' and 'the manual exit name'.
    a text called 'the exit value assert' is 'gen assert number is' of "PRC-62" and 'the manual exit name' and 'the exit code'.
    a text called 'the manual signal name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "manual signal".
    a text called 'the manual signal line' is "a number called {'the manual signal name'} is {'the status name'} bit-and 127".
    a text called 'the function signal name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "function signal".
    a text called 'the function signal line' is "a number called {'the function signal name'} is 'signal of' of {'the status name'}".
    a text called 'the signal agree assert' is 'gen assert number matches' of "PRC-63" and 'the function signal name' and 'the manual signal name'.
    a text called 'the signal zero assert' is 'gen assert number is' of "PRC-62" and 'the manual signal name' and 0.
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the child line', 'the child branch', 'the reap line', 'the status line', 'the manual exit line', 'the function exit line', 'the exit agree assert', 'the exit value assert', 'the manual signal line', 'the function signal line', 'the signal agree assert', 'the signal zero assert'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(PRC-33: `Execute "<path>".` performs execve(2), replacing the current
 process image entirely - the manual's own example shows the line after
 it never running (LANGUAGE.md:4298-4312). SAFETY (this surface brief;
 PROCEDURE.md sect.6's Execute carve-out): the target is drawn from a
 FIXED two-element allowlist, /usr/bin/true and /usr/bin/false, and
 nothing else, ever - no generated command line, no path built from a
 variable. The child forks, execs one of the two, and the parent reaps
 it and decodes the exit code the manual's own decoder predicts (0 for
 true, 1 for false) - an oracle the generator can check because it
 chose which binary ran.)
To 'gen leaf process execute' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    Set gen_process_has_reaped to true.
    a number called 'the program draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a text called 'the program' is "/usr/bin/true".
    a number called 'the expected exit' is 0.
    If 'the program draw' is 1 then,
        Set 'the program' to "/usr/bin/false".
    If 'the program draw' is 1 then,
        Set 'the expected exit' to 1.
    a text called 'the child name' is 'gen process witness'.
    a text called 'the child line' is "a number called {'the child name'} is fork the process".
    a text called 'the exec branch' is "If {'the child name'} is 0 then, Execute \"{'the program'}\"".
    a text called 'the reap name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "exec reaped".
    a text called 'the reap line' is "a number called {'the reap name'} is reap child {'the child name'}".
    a text called 'the exit name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "exec exit code".
    a text called 'the exit line' is "a number called {'the exit name'} is the reaped status divide 256 modulo 256".
    a text called 'the assert line' is 'gen assert number is' of "PRC-33" and 'the exit name' and 'the expected exit'.
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the child line', 'the exec branch', 'the reap line', 'the exit line', 'the assert line'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(PRC-72, PRC-73, PRC-75: `Send signal <N> to process <pid>.` performs
 kill(2) (LANGUAGE.md:4482-4483); `child` is an accepted alias for
 `process` (LANGUAGE.md:4484); signal 0 delivers nothing but errors only
 if no process has that pid, the standard existence check
 (LANGUAGE.md:4499-4500), and a successful send clears the error flag
 (LANGUAGE.md:4490). SAFETY (this surface brief): the target is ALWAYS
 signal 0, and ALWAYS the pid this leaf's own `fork` just returned -
 never a drawn number, never the process's own group. The pid stays
 valid (a live child, or a zombie awaiting reap) until this leaf reaps
 it, so the existence check always succeeds regardless of how fast the
 exec'd program finished. A foreign, deliberately-failing reap first
 sets the error flag, so the successful signal right after it proves
 PRC-73's "clears the flag" rather than merely "does not set a fresh
 one".)
To 'gen leaf process signal existence check' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    Set gen_process_has_reaped to true.
    a number called 'the program draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a text called 'the program' is "/usr/bin/true".
    If 'the program draw' is 1 then,
        Set 'the program' to "/usr/bin/false".
    a text called 'the child name' is 'gen process witness'.
    a text called 'the child line' is "a number called {'the child name'} is fork the process".
    a text called 'the exec branch' is "If {'the child name'} is 0 then, Execute \"{'the program'}\"".
    a number called 'the alias draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a text called 'the target word' is "process".
    If 'the alias draw' is 1 then,
        Set 'the target word' to "child".
    a number called 'the foreign pid' is 'rng below' of 900000 add 9000000.
    a text called 'the stale reap name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "stale reap".
    a text called 'the stale reap line' is "a number called {'the stale reap name'} is reap process {'the foreign pid'}".
    a text called 'the stale flag name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "stale reap failed".
    a text called 'the stale flag init' is "a boolean called {'the stale flag name'} is false".
    a text called 'the stale handler' is "On error Set {'the stale flag name'} to true".
    a text called 'the stale assert' is 'gen assert true' of "PRC-49" and 'the stale flag name'.
    a text called 'the signal flag name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "signal failed".
    a text called 'the signal flag init' is "a boolean called {'the signal flag name'} is false".
    a text called 'the signal line' is "Send signal 0 to {'the target word'} {'the child name'}".
    a text called 'the signal handler' is "On error Set {'the signal flag name'} to true".
