(PRC-47, PRC-48: `reap process <pid-expr>` / `reap child <pid-expr>` both
 `wait4(2)` a SPECIFIC pid, both spellings (LANGUAGE.md:4334-4335); reap
 returns a negative value on error, on any reap form (LANGUAGE.md:4333)
 - one leaf reaps a REAL forked
 child this way (drawn spelling, asserted the returned pid equals the
 forked one and the decoded exit code matches what the child was told to
 report) and the other reaps a reserved-invalid pid the same way,
 asserting only what the manual documents: negative, not a specific
 value (PRC-47 is hand-verified as exactly -10, but only "negative" is a
 claim the manual makes - see docs/ledger/process-control.md's own note
 on this row). The reserved-invalid pid reuses the exact "past any real
 pid_max" idiom PRC-49 already established in this file (kind 265)
 rather than inventing a second one - that range is PINNED by the
 requirement that it can never collide with a live pid, not a magnitude
 CLAUDE.md's extreme-literal rule asks this leaf to widen.)
