(HELD OUT, kind 352, unregistered - candidate found this batch, reported
 in full in REPORT-LEAVES-PROCESS-B.md: under RANDOM layout, seed 1006
 (budget 12) puts a single newline between a reap expression and the
 `without waiting` suffix, and the compiler then refuses the program -
 `Expected a statement, got Without` - even on the SAME construct that
 compiles cleanly on one line, hand-verified repeatedly this session.
 Minimal repro (3 lines, no leaf involved):
   a number called r is reap process 5
   without waiting.
   Print r.
 fails; the same two lines joined ("...reap process 5 without waiting.")
 compiles and runs. `print ... without newline` - the OTHER `without`
 suffix in the language - tolerates the identical newline split fine, so
 this looks narrow to the reap-suffix's own grammar production rather
 than a general newline rule; LANGUAGE.md:226 states plainly that only a
 period closes a clause, which this appears to contradict. This is a
 layout-randomiser interaction (docs/ledger/PROCEDURE.md sect.5): the
 leaf below is complete, correct Vox and hand-verifies clean under both
 pinned compilers with ordinary formatting; it is left UNREGISTERED
 because the campaign's own layout pass can turn its output into this.
 PRC-55 (the one sub-claim here that does not need the suffix at all) is
 salvaged into 'gen leaf process reaped ordinary identifier' below
 instead, so it is not lost to this same hold.

 PRC-50, PRC-51, PRC-52, PRC-53, PRC-54, PRC-55: any reap form takes a
 `without waiting` suffix (WNOHANG) (LANGUAGE.md:4342-4349); the three
 outcomes are told apart by the return value alone - a child that
 finished returns its pid with the flag clear (LANGUAGE.md:4354), a
 child that exists but has not finished returns exactly 0 with the flag
 clear, NOT an error (LANGUAGE.md:4355-4356), and a genuine error (no
 such child) returns negative with the flag set (LANGUAGE.md:4357-4358).
 A poll that returns 0 reaps nothing and so does not disturb `the reaped
 status` (LANGUAGE.md:4360-4362). `without` is already reserved (the
 `print ... without newline` token) so the suffix cannot be confused
 with a call argument, and `waiting` remains an ordinary identifier
 everywhere it is not this exact suffix (LANGUAGE.md:4362-4365).

 SAFETY DEVIATION from the ledger's own retained probe
 (docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-50.vox): that probe forces the
 "still running" observation with `Send signal 9` to the slow child
 before reaping it. This surface brief's standing policy restricts `Send
 signal` to signal 0 on a program's own live child ONLY, so this leaf
 gets the same observation a different way instead: the forked child
 `Wait`s a drawn interval before exiting, and the parent's FIRST poll
 (issued with no delay at all, right after the fork) is guaranteed to
 land before that interval elapses; a second poll, issued after the
 parent itself has waited comfortably longer than the child's interval,
 is then guaranteed to land after the child exited. Hand-verified this
 session, five back-to-back runs plus a deliberately-broken run, both
 pinned compilers, no flake: the child's own wait is drawn 100-399ms and
 the parent's second wait is that same draw plus a fixed 500ms margin,
 so the ordering is deterministic BY CONSTRUCTION, not by luck, even
 though the exact millisecond values vary every time this leaf is drawn
 - only the 500ms MARGIN is a fixed implementation detail (not a manual
 claim), the same way the retained probe's own fixed 300ms margin is
 documented as "not a claim about scheduling".

 The genuine-ECHILD probe (PRC-53) needs no live child at all - a
 reserved-invalid pid can never be this program's child - so it runs
 first, standalone, reusing the same "past any real pid_max" idiom
 PRC-47/48 above and PRC-49 (kind 265) already established. Every reap
 here also updates gen_process_has_reaped, the same shared per-program
 flag every other reaping kind in this file maintains, for PRC-58's
 sentinel claim elsewhere.)
To 'gen leaf process reap without waiting' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    Set gen_process_has_reaped to true.
    a text called 'the waiting value' is 'gen extreme number'.
    a text called 'the waiting line' is "a number called waiting is {'the waiting value'}".
    a number called 'the foreign pid' is 'rng below' of 900000 add 9000000.
    a number called 'the echild spelling draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a text called 'the echild expr' is "reap process {'the foreign pid'} without waiting".
    If 'the echild spelling draw' is 1 then,
        Set 'the echild expr' to "reap child {'the foreign pid'} without waiting".
    a text called 'the echild result' is 'gen buffer companion' of "echild poll".
    a text called 'the echild flag' is 'gen buffer companion' of "echild refused".
    a text called 'the echild flag init' is "a boolean called {'the echild flag'} is false".
    a text called 'the echild line' is "a number called {'the echild result'} is {'the echild expr'}".
    a text called 'the echild handler' is "On error Set {'the echild flag'} to true".
    a text called 'the echild got shown' is 'gen buffer slot of' of 'the echild result'.
    a text called 'the echild negative assert' is "If {'the echild result'} is not less than 0 then, Print \"ASSERT PRC-53: expected negative got {'the echild got shown'}\", Exit 95. Print {'the echild result'}".
    a text called 'the echild flag assert' is 'gen assert true' of "PRC-53" and 'the echild flag'.
    a number called 'the exit code' is 'gen process safe exit code'.
    a number called 'the child wait' is 'rng below' of 300 add 100.
    a number called 'the parent wait' is 'the child wait' add 500.
    a text called 'the child name' is 'gen process witness'.
    a text called 'the child line' is "a number called {'the child name'} is fork the process".
    a text called 'the child branch' is "If {'the child name'} is 0 then, Wait {'the child wait'} milliseconds, Exit {'the exit code'}".
    a text called 'the before status' is 'gen buffer companion' of "status before poll".
    a text called 'the before status line' is "a number called {'the before status'} is the reaped status".
    a number called 'the poll spelling draw' is 'rng below' of 3.
    a text called 'the poll expr' is "reap any child process without waiting".
    If 'the poll spelling draw' is 1 then,
        Set 'the poll expr' to "reap child {'the child name'} without waiting".
    If 'the poll spelling draw' is 2 then,
        Set 'the poll expr' to "reap process {'the child name'} without waiting".
    a text called 'the immediate result' is 'gen buffer companion' of "immediate poll".
    a text called 'the immediate flag' is 'gen buffer companion' of "immediate refused".
    a text called 'the immediate flag init' is "a boolean called {'the immediate flag'} is false".
    a text called 'the immediate line' is "a number called {'the immediate result'} is {'the poll expr'}".
    a text called 'the immediate handler' is "On error Set {'the immediate flag'} to true".
    a text called 'the immediate zero assert' is 'gen assert number is' of "PRC-52" and 'the immediate result' and 0.
    a text called 'the immediate flag assert' is 'gen assert false' of "PRC-52" and 'the immediate flag'.
    a text called 'the after status' is 'gen buffer companion' of "status after poll".
    a text called 'the after status line' is "a number called {'the after status'} is the reaped status".
    a text called 'the unchanged assert' is 'gen assert number matches' of "PRC-54" and 'the after status' and 'the before status'.
    a text called 'the wait line' is "Wait {'the parent wait'} milliseconds".
    a text called 'the later result' is 'gen buffer companion' of "later poll".
    a text called 'the later flag' is 'gen buffer companion' of "later refused".
    a text called 'the later flag init' is "a boolean called {'the later flag'} is false".
    a text called 'the later line' is "a number called {'the later result'} is {'the poll expr'}".
    a text called 'the later handler' is "On error Set {'the later flag'} to true".
    (Asserted as a BOOLEAN, not by printing the poll result - see the same
     note above 'the real match assert' in 'gen leaf process reap by pid':
     that result IS the real OS pid, and printing it would make this
     leaf's output vary run to run even at a fixed seed.)
    a text called 'the later matched name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "later poll matched".
    a text called 'the later matched init' is "a boolean called {'the later matched name'} is false".
    a text called 'the later matched set' is "If {'the later result'} is {'the child name'} then, Set {'the later matched name'} to true".
    a text called 'the later match assert' is 'gen assert true' of "PRC-51" and 'the later matched name'.
    a text called 'the later flag assert' is 'gen assert false' of "PRC-51" and 'the later flag'.
    a number called 'the waiting expected' is 'the waiting value' as a number.
    a text called 'the waiting assert' is 'gen assert number is' of "PRC-55" and "waiting" and 'the waiting expected'.
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the waiting line', 'the echild flag init', 'the echild line', 'the echild handler', 'the echild negative assert', 'the echild flag assert', 'the child line', 'the child branch', 'the before status line', 'the immediate flag init', 'the immediate line', 'the immediate handler', 'the immediate zero assert', 'the immediate flag assert', 'the after status line', 'the unchanged assert', 'the wait line', 'the later flag init', 'the later line', 'the later handler', 'the later matched init', 'the later matched set', 'the later match assert', 'the later flag assert', 'the waiting assert'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(PRC-60, PRC-61: `reaped` stays an ordinary identifier everywhere it is
 not the exact phrase `the reaped status` - `the reaped` followed by
 anything else is an ordinary variable reference too
 (LANGUAGE.md:4384-4386). `tests/102_fork_reap.vox` does `Set reaped to
 reap any child process.` and keeps passing (LANGUAGE.md:4386-4387); this
 leaf reproduces that exact body (a bare, undeclared `reaped` receiving a
 reap result via `Set ... to ...`, which the manual's own retained test
 relies on working) rather than merely declaring `reaped` unused, and
 then reads the REAL `the reaped status` phrase alongside a `'the
 reaped'` quoted two-word variable holding unrelated text, proving all
 three coexist without the parser confusing any of them.

 PRC-55 folded in here rather than living with the `without waiting`
 family above: its own claim ("`waiting` remains an ordinary identifier
 everywhere it is not this suffix", LANGUAGE.md:4362-4365) needs no reap
 call at all to test - only a plain declaration and a read-back - so it
 is not affected by that family's held-out candidate and does not need
 to wait on it.)
To 'gen leaf process reaped ordinary identifier' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    Set gen_process_has_reaped to true.
    a number called 'the exit code' is 'gen process safe exit code'.
    a text called 'the child name' is 'gen process witness'.
    a text called 'the child line' is "a number called {'the child name'} is fork the process".
    a text called 'the child branch' is "If {'the child name'} is 0 then, Exit {'the exit code'}".
    a text called 'the bare set line' is "Set reaped to reap any child process".
    (Asserted as a BOOLEAN, not by printing `reaped` directly - see the
     same note above 'the real match assert' in
     'gen leaf process reap by pid': `reaped` here holds the real OS pid
     the fork returned, and printing it would make this leaf's own
     output vary run to run even at a fixed seed.)
    a text called 'the matched name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "reap matched".
    a text called 'the matched init' is "a boolean called {'the matched name'} is false".
    a text called 'the matched set' is "If reaped is {'the child name'} then, Set {'the matched name'} to true".
    a text called 'the match assert' is 'gen assert true' of "PRC-61" and 'the matched name'.
    a text called 'the decoded name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "reproduced exit".
    a text called 'the decoded line' is "a number called {'the decoded name'} is the reaped status divide 256 modulo 256".
    a text called 'the decoded assert' is 'gen assert number is' of "PRC-60" and 'the decoded name' and 'the exit code'.
    a text called 'the quoted phrase word' is 'gen word from' of gen_type_words.
    a text called 'the quoted phrase line' is "a text called 'the reaped' is \"{'the quoted phrase word'}\"".
    a text called 'the quoted phrase assert' is "If 'the reaped' is not \"{'the quoted phrase word'}\" then, Print \"ASSERT PRC-60: expected {'the quoted phrase word'} got {{'the reaped'}}\", Exit 95. Print 'the reaped'".
    a text called 'the waiting value' is 'gen extreme number'.
    a number called 'the waiting expected' is 'the waiting value' as a number.
    a text called 'the waiting line' is "a number called waiting is {'the waiting value'}".
    a text called 'the waiting assert' is 'gen assert number is' of "PRC-55" and "waiting" and 'the waiting expected'.
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the child line', 'the child branch', 'the bare set line', 'the matched init', 'the matched set', 'the match assert', 'the decoded line', 'the decoded assert', 'the quoted phrase line', 'the quoted phrase assert', 'the waiting line', 'the waiting assert'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(PRC-87: undocumented precision, not a manual sentence - every
 path-taking statement in this section accepts an empty path and fails
 cleanly through the error flag rather than crashing; the memory-safety
 floor for the whole section, and the first degenerate input a leaf will
 produce by accident. This leaf sticks to the three unbanned, non-policy-
 restricted constructs already registered elsewhere in this file - create
 directory, remove directory, symbolic link - and draws which one gets
 the empty path this call, rather than emitting all three every time,
 since the OTHER two still get their ordinary confined exercise from
 kinds 260/263 in the same campaign. `Mount`/`Unmount` (emit-safe but
 covered by kind 262 already) and `Execute` (locked to the fixed
 true/false allowlist by this surface brief's policy, so an empty path is
 not a value this leaf is allowed to hand it) are left out; `Pivot root`
 stays banned. The ledger's own retained probe,
 docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-87.vox, sweeps all eight
 constructs the manual lists in one hand-verification pass; this leaf
 draws one of the three per call so the corpus varies which construct is
 exercised, rather than repeating a fixed eight-statement shape every
 time it is drawn.)
To 'gen leaf process empty path refusal' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a number called 'the construct draw' is 'rng below' of 3.
    a text called 'the flag name' is 'gen process witness'.
    a text called 'the flag init' is "a boolean called {'the flag name'} is false".
    a text called 'the handler' is "On error Set {'the flag name'} to true".
    a text called 'the assert line' is 'gen assert true' of "PRC-87" and 'the flag name'.
    a text called 'the continued' is "Print \"execution continued\"".
    a text called 'the statement' is "Create a directory called \"\"".
    If 'the construct draw' is 1 then,
        Set 'the statement' to "Remove the directory called \"\"".
    If 'the construct draw' is 2 then,
        Set 'the statement' to "Create symbolic link from \"\" to \"\"".
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the flag init', 'the statement', 'the handler', 'the assert line', 'the continued'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.
